    "## Query refinement loop\n",
    "\n",
    "The eval slice mixes retrieval-quality labels. CRAG only rewrites the query and re-retrieves when the cross-encoder labels a retrieval **AMBIGUOUS** (or **INCORRECT** within the retry budget). Rows that started **CORRECT** stay at one retrieval round, which acts as a negative control that refinement isn't fired indiscriminately.\n",
    "\n",
    "The comparison table below merges baseline labels with CRAG labels per question so the rows where refinement actually fired (and whether they improved) are easy to spot.\n"
   ]
  },
