    "## M2 micro-demo (cells above) vs M3 canonical ablation\n",
    "\n",
    "The executable cells above are a **pedagogical `n = 10` walkthrough** on a BGE-M3 mini-index: they show how the evaluator, refinement loop, and τ-sweep machinery work end-to-end. Those numbers (**60% → 80% correct rate**) came from a hand-picked mixed slice and must **not** be quoted as the project headline.\n",
    "\n",
    "**M3 canonical numbers** come from `scripts/run_crag_ablation.py` on the **full gold set** (97 questions incl. 9 unanswerable), retriever `e5_large_coarse_rerank`, `k = 10`, with **Option A abstain** wired in `corrective_rag.py` (INCORRECT / exhausted-AMBIGUOUS → empty context + explicit abstain message; no web fallback).\n",
    "\n",
    "The cell below loads a committed sweep JSON if present; otherwise it prints the CLI to reproduce on RCP/SCITAS.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Headline partition (τ_high = 0.7, τ_low = 0.4 — latency-optimal cell)\n",
    "\n",
    "Report-integrated numbers (post adapter-text fix, PR #72 / #73):\n",
    "\n",
    "| quantity | value |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| baseline direct-correct retrieval | **0.876** (85/97) |\n",
    "| branch distribution | **{correct: 85, ambiguous: 9, incorrect: 3}** |\n",
    "| refinement upside cap | **+9.3 pp** (rescue all 9 ambiguous in one round) |\n",
    "| abstain strict (INCORRECT only) | n=3, precision=0.33, recall=0.11 (1/9 unanswerables) |\n",
    "| abstain loose (+ AMBIGUOUS) | n=12, precision=0.25, recall=0.33 |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Methodological caveats (for the report)\n",
    "\n",
    "- **τ_l is the operative knob**; sweeping τ_high ∈ {0.6, 0.7, 0.8} moves at most three borderline queries.\n",
    "- The ms-marco-MiniLM cross-encoder scores **7/9 unanswerables above τ_high** because lexical overlap with retrieved chunks masquerades as evidence — this bounds abstain recall and motivates corpus-only grounding (no web fallback).\n",
    "- A prior RCP run collapsed every question to INCORRECT because `RetrieverAdapter.search` dropped chunk `text`; fixed in PR #72. Always ensure adapter hits include `text` before trusting confidences.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Driver for graders / teammates\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "uv sync --all-packages\n",
    "uv run python -m scripts.run_crag_ablation \\\n",
    "  --retriever-config e5_large_coarse_rerank \\\n",
    "  --probe-cache evaluation/crag/results/probe_cache.json \\\n",
    "  --output evaluation/crag/results/threshold_sweep.json\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Probe cache makes re-sweeps cheap (seconds) after the one-time retrieve+score pass.\n"
